### Test Case 2: Apparent Wind Vector Algebra
* **Objective:** Verify vector-component calculations of Apparent Wind Speed (AWS), Apparent Wind Direction (AWD), and Apparent Wind Angle (AWA) using the nautical vector formula: $\vec{V}_a = \vec{V}_t - \vec{V}_b$.
* **Execution Result:** ✅ **PASSED**
* **Formulae Verified:**
  * $V_{t,x} = \text{TWS} \cdot \sin(\text{TWD}_{rad})$
  * $V_{t,y} = \text{TWS} \cdot \cos(\text{TWD}_{rad})$
  * $V_{a,x} = V_{t,x} - V_{b,x}$
  * $V_{a,y} = V_{t,y} - V_{b,y}$
  * $\text{AWS} = \sqrt{V_{a,x}^2 + V_{a,y}^2}$
  * $\text{AWA} = \text{AWD} - \text{Heading}$

